  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Corrects DotCall fallback participation and Grace composition across the parser, elaborator, evaluator, editor model, optimizer gates, Lean model, tests, and documentation. Ordinary dotted calls remain structural-first with ordinary lexical fallback. `a~.t(args)` is ordinary postfix Grace on receiver name `a` followed by ordinary dot; `a.~t(args)` is ordinary prefix Grace on the participating fallback/member occurrence `t`. Both elaborate to the same DotCall body as `a.t(args)`, while the two-name inferred order is `(t, a)` instead of ordinary `(a, t)`. A may-selected fallback participates at semantic source position (receiver, member/fallback, arguments), independently of runtime fallback invocation order. Grace remains restricted to one bare name occurrence and affects only inferred parameter ordering. Removes the provisional runtime-extension public surface shipped in 0.8.159 (`DotResolutionMode`, `Expr.DotCall.ResolutionMode`, `Expr.DotCall.ExtensionMarkerSpan`, `DotCallContext.IsExtension`, and `AstWalker.VisitExtensionDotMarker`) and the later `Expr.Grace.IsExtensionReceiver` provenance flag; this is an intentional source/binary compatibility correction because those members represented semantic state that no longer exists.",
